From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Express unchanged MIT license using PEP 621 file metadata
Source: https://github.com/dgilland/pydash/blob/f46de3669742c075e5379c1e193c86c1c2c70dc2/pyproject.toml
Original-License: MIT
Applies-To: Pydash 8.1.0; selected target setuptools 68.0.0
Upstream-Status: Downstream compatibility only; not submitted upstream
Root-Cause: The setuptools 68 validator requires a PEP 621 license file/text table
Removal-Condition: Verified target selected setuptools >= 77 supports the original expression

The fixed upstream pyproject uses a PEP 639 license expression string.
The target setuptools 68 backend accepts the original PEP 621 file/text
table shape. Refer to the unmodified complete LICENSE.rst instead.
Build-system requirements, license text, runtime and default tests are
unchanged. Remove when the selected target backend supports the upstream
expression (setuptools >= 77). Target build success is not yet observed.

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ dynamic = ["version"]
 authors = [{ name = "Derrick Gilland", email = "dgilland@gmail.com" }]
 description = 'The kitchen sink of Python utility libraries for doing "stuff" in a functional way. Based on the Lo-Dash Javascript library.'
 readme = "README.rst"
-license = "MIT"
+license = {file = "LICENSE.rst"}
 keywords = ["pydash", "utility", "functional", "lodash", "underscore"]
 classifiers = [
     "Development Status :: 5 - Production/Stable",
